  "scope": "# Review \u2014 db95939a5dd0 v3.2.0\n- Defect: request overrides leaked into priors, malformed requests were accepted, lawful fixtures were misdeclared, and lessons could leave a global-per-color direction rival alive.\n- Repair: validate before RNG construction, make explicit `None` identical to omission, mark fixtures lawful, and teach the local top/bottom role with an opposite-role color-reuse witness.\n- Lesson contract: 3 demonstrations + 1 query; production uses ordered windows from a period-2 default schedule; all 4 cyclic query positions are required.\n- Production verdict: 12/12 materialized lessons identifiable; 0 hook errors.\n- Rotation verdict: 48/48 query rotations identifiable; larger census 1,200/1,200 clean across 300 lessons and 3 bands.\n- Checks: 94/94 focused tests passed; final battery 12/12 stages green; override matrix 15,210 draws with 0 findings and 0 warnings.\n- Final generator SHA-256: `7bf7cef69b27cf6507efc9239c4575a0b940d867eb0462e622cc0450bcf825b1`; canonical `RULE_HASH` remains `a742202e03fb`.\n- Racket authority: two selected `target_code` records were synchronized to canonical exact text; behavior and rule hash did not change, and archival `raw_code` was preserved.\n- Remaining blocker: none; finite rival coverage and the deliberate period-2 support schedule remain documented limitations.\n- Acceptance: routine.\n\n## What changed\n",
